  <title>Project 9 Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02533</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Project 9 Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d08a32f9-f0a5-470b-9019-e9fe0a6f8ab1</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this culminating project, you will synthesize methods of solving quadratic equations and graphing quadratic functions to answer questions about within a context. You will use tools learned throughout the unit to grapple with solving problems about a quadratic function that represents a context. Since this work requires using what you know to tackle an unfamiliar problem, you will need to make sense of problems and demonstrate perseverance.
</para>
<para>Technology isn't required for this lesson, but there are opportunities for you  to choose to use appropriate technology to solve problems. 
</para>
<title>Project Activities</title>
<list type="enumerated">
  <item>Equations of Two Lines and a Curve </item>
  <item>Analyzing a Dive </item>
  <item>A Linear Function and a Quadratic Function </item>
  <item>Profit from a River Cruise </item>
</list>
<title>Learning Targets</title> 
<para>When you finish this project, you will have demonstrated how to:
</para>
<list>
  <item>Interpret information about a quadratic function given its equation or a graph.
  </item>
  <item>Rewrite quadratic functions in different but equivalent forms of my choosing and use that form to solve problems.
  </item>
  <item>Decide which quadratic form to use depending on the questions being asked.
  </item>
</list>


</section>
</content>
</document>
